codex
The first executable check exposed a backend limitation: K’s Haskell prover cannot evaluate the built-in floating-point conversion hook. Since the assignment explicitly asks for our own semantics, I’m replacing that dependency with an exact rational model for decimal values. This also makes symbolic proofs stronger and backend-independent instead of relying on unsupported IEEE-float hooks.
